**Theorem 6.3 (four individual exact kernels).** Separately for every
$V\in\{S,T,B,M\}$ and all $h,k\in\Omega$,

$$
V(h)=V(k)\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad h\sim_{Q_+}k.
\tag{CSA.6}
$$

Proof. For $S$, equal supports give equal raw $Y$ by Lemma 3.4. Extract
CSA.4 and apply Lemma 5.4 to obtain $h=k$, hence equal task maps by
Lemma 6.2. In the reverse direction task equivalence gives $h=k$ by
Lemma 6.2 and therefore equal supports. These are both inclusions for $S$.

For $B$, prefix closure gives the identical whole support independently
from that boundary. Lemma 3.4, extraction and identification again give
$h=k$ and task equivalence. Conversely task equivalence gives $h=k$ and
therefore identical terminal antichains. These are both inclusions for $B$.

For $T$, erase each actual patch occurrence to its native occurrence,
including its actual input, operands, labels and receipt. This gives
exactly $h$ by CSA.3, so equal temporal words give equal task maps.
Conversely task equivalence gives $h=k$, whose literal compiler entries,
operand occurrences and auxiliary construction roles coincide. Hence their
actual ordered patch words agree. These are both inclusions for $T$.

For $M$, equal selected memory structures give equal extracted keys by
Lemma 5.3, equal histories by Lemma 5.4, and equal task maps by Lemma 6.2.
Conversely task equivalence gives identical histories, hence exactly the
same selected retained material, frontier and actual rights. These are
both inclusions for $M$. No intersection of four insufficient kernels
has been used. ∎

